WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.000
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.800
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.430
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.140
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.140
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.860
This time...

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:13.730
Okay.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.440
Blackjack!

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.780
Hooray! I won five times in a row!

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.780
Damn! I lost again!

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:23.200
You lost again?

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.950
You're so weak.

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.050
What is it?

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:35.960
What's wrong?

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.800
How did she get in?

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:57.990
It's mine.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.110
Damn! How dare she!

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:13.000
Caught like a mouse in a trap! Or should I say bat?

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.340
Hands up in the air!

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.640
She's not here.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:26.220
Where is she?

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.770
Dammit. Search over there.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:28.890
Okay.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.060
No one's there.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.350
What?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:41.490
Dammit, where did she go?

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:02.340
It's beautiful, though it's nowhere near sparkling as a Chaos Emerald.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:06.050
I'm going to do whatever it takes to get a Chaos Emerald!

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:11.500
Episode 11

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:11.500
The Beautiful, Mysterious Thief Rouge

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:20.030
Last night, the world's largest diamond on exhibit at the National Museum was stolen.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:30.910
Judging by the thief's bold escape, authorities believe it is the same thief from the recent string of gem thefts.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.580
Reporting from on site, this is Scarlet Garcia for SSTV.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.380
Sonic?

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.960
He's not here either.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:45.340
Sonic went out with Tails and Chris.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.850
I see... Will you eat this with me?

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.720
Are you sure you don't mind?

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.890
Of course not. Let's eat it while it's still hot.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.810
Okay!

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.610
There's no signal yet?

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.910
Umm...

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.870
Not yet.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.870
We have to find the remaining five before Eggman.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.670
Isn't that right, Sonic?

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:25.550
Sonic, where are you? Sonic!

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:31.970
I've had enough.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:38.020
Our enemy Dr. Eggman is threatening our nation. We're launching an all-out attack on his headquarters.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:43.070
But is our military strong enough to defeat him?

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:47.610
We salvaged and analyzed Dr. Eggman's robot.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:54.080
His technology is not only superior to ours, but to every other country in the world.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.920
That doesn't mean we should sit around and do nothing.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.960
Sonic's cooperation is essential.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:02.590
Sonic?

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:11.220
The only one who managed to stop Dr. Eggman's activities was an unidentified creature named Sonic.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.970
If we can bring him to our side, we may have a chance.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:20.270
But will this Sonic negotiate with us?

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.730
We already verified that he understands the human language.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.570
I will make him agree.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.240
Okay, I'll allow it.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.910
Thank you very much.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:50.050
Hey, is that the Chaos Emerald that Sonic and his friends are looking for?

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.180
Yeah.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.760
I hope they find it.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:56.220
I don't care if you talk so long as you keep moving your hands.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.770
Oops, sorry!

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.020
Is that an emerald?

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:03.900
Y-Yeah.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:08.240
Aren't emeralds supposed to be green?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:11.610
Oh yeah, you're right. I have to recolor it.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:15.080
No, it's okay. Use any color you like.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:21.290
Come to think of it, I heard that a red emerald was found in Silky Heights.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:24.340
I'm sorry.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:31.340
If I'm not mistaken, it was found in an abandoned factory in Silky Heights.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:38.060
I only came to see how Sonic was doing, but I got great info.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:46.440
Chris, wait up!

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.200
I'm Danny. Nice to meet you.

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:56.660
I'm Amy. Nice to meet you too. And this is Tails.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:58.080
Hi.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:58.700
Hey.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.790
Huh? Where's Sonic?

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.380
He just left. I think we should get going too.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:14.930
Takeoff!

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:33.990
It's to the right.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:41.200
Awesome! This is awesome, Chris!

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.960
I get it, so calm down, Danny.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.750
There's Sonic.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.680
They fell for it.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:18.820
There it is. I guess I'll go get it.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.140
A glass ball?

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:53.900
Oh, it's a trap.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:55.400
Don't move!

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.240
All right, all right.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.290
So you like to play rough?

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.160
What?

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.380
What are you laughing about?!

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:11.960
Commander!

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.250
Oh, umm... I'm sorry.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:21.100
I won't try to escape. I just don't want my flawless skin damaged.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:23.140
Forget the handcuffs.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:26.980
What's your name?

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.480
Rouge. Rouge the Bat.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.730
I've seen you before...

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:38.320
That's right! You're the one who stole the diamond from the National Museum.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:39.820
I guess so.

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:46.620
We set a trap to capture Sonic, but we caught someone unexpected instead.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.270
Aren't you hungry?

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:13.230
Yeah.

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.450
Don't they even serve coffee here?

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:24.070
Are you aware of the situation you're in?

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.830
I'm the beautiful girl who was kidnapped

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:30.410
and you're the old lady who kidnapped me.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.420
Old lady? You've gotta be kidding!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.840
Topaz, serve her coffee.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:38.960
Aye aye, sir!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.510
Why do I have to do this?

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:49.520
So your name's Topaz? That's the name of a gemstone.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:01.820
You're pretty noisy.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.620
I'm sorry.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.030
Ms. Rouge?

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:07.530
Hi.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:12.660
You seem awfully relaxed despite the fact that the authorities have a warrant for your arrest.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:17.090
I'll get right to the point. Do you want to make a deal?

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:19.050
A deal?

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:25.300
We will grant you immunity from the jewel robberies if you work on our staff in exchange.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:28.260
When you say staff, do you mean as a secretary?

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:31.770
As an agent working directly for the President.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:36.150
Wow! You're making a jewel thief into a government official?

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:40.730
Are you sure you want to do this? Do you think the taxpayers will allow this?

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:44.660
That's not for you to worry about. What's your answer?

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:46.870
Let me think...

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:52.160
If I'm an agent, it will be easier to get information on the Chaos Emerald.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:54.830
Fine. It sounds interesting.

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:58.040
We're counting on you, Ms. Rouge.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.920
Do I have to give you back the diamond?

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:07.390
Who knows...

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:11.890
The case is still unsolved, so I don't think they'll ever find the diamond.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.350
That's the situation.

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:23.650
I guess I'll try going left.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:44.630
What's this?

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:46.300
It's a bomb.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.340
A bomb?

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:51.350
If I push this button on the remote control, it will explode.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:56.480
No offense, but we still don't trust you.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.650
I thought you liked jewels.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.610
I hate fake ones.

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:04.650
Why would we use real ones if we're going to blow it up?

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:08.570
Anyway, look how tacky this is! Did you choose it?

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.620
What do you mean by that?

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:12.370
Exactly what you think.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:14.660
Want me to push the switch?

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:16.330
Will you two stop already?

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.040
We're approaching the drop zone.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.340
Okay, understood! Let's go.

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:40.400
Sheesh. There's nothing here.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:43.320
Was the information fake?

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:46.900
More importantly, I wonder who messed with the sign.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.110
Beats me.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.750
Where's the entrance?

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.470
Damn, I don't have the slightest idea.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:13.010
This is so annoying!

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:18.520
Damn!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:19.980
Wait!

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:21.520
Let's go.

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:38.160
This way.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:39.910
Wait! Where are you going?

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:44.000
I know the way. I snuck in here before.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.250
Really?

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.880
Why would I lie?

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.760
Fine, wait a sec.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.800
Okay, let's go.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:27.210
The map is almost complete. All that's left is the location of the power station.

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:29.420
If you know where, tell us!

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:32.470
I'm not interested in engines.

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:36.850
What should we do? It's almost dawn.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.310
We have no choice. Let's retreat.

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:50.320
Wait!

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:53.740
I'm going to look around a little more.

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.780
We can't let you go alone.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:58.580
I know. I'll be right back.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.080
I'll go with her.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.500
You're only going to get in my way.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:04.210
Fine.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.170
Both of you, don't do anything reckless.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:11.050
Yes sir!

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.300
Aye aye, sir!

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.610
I'm sure this is the place.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:32.070
Step back or you'll get hurt.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:44.000
Is this the power station?

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:51.460
There it is!

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.630
Chaos Emerald.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:58.930
It's beautiful.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.100
Is this really the power station?

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:20.160
Help!

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:21.870
What a klutz!

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:31.170
Screw Kick!

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.430
What's that sound?

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:47.600
What's the racket so early in the morning?

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.650
Is this ultrasound?

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:08.870
No! I'm afraid! Don't…

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:16.050
Somebody help me! My head is going to crack!

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:23.140
These cries are from E-70. That means something must have happened at the storage vault housing the Chaos Emerald.

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:25.310
Go, guard robot!

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:27.970
Anyway, it's so loud!

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:33.730
I'm scared!

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:35.570
I have to do something.

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:50.370
Rouge!

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:55.590
That's the power station.

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:00.970
Screw Kick!

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:09.520
I'm scared!

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:15.400
You're annoying me.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:35.290
The Chaos Emerald!

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:36.290
Stop!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.340
I hate this!

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:42.420
You're so noisy.

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:44.430
That's right.

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:03.740
Topaz, push the switch!

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:20.670
Screw Kick!

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:24.630
We're leaving.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:32.270
Out of my way!

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:32.770
Right!

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:33.520
I'm sorry.

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:36.480
Who are you?

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:58.830
Thank you, Rouge.

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.130
No problem.

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:02.050
But you're heavy.

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:08.590
You'll pay for this…

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:16.640
Chris...

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:18.310
Danny...

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:20.730
The information is fake!

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:24.480
Oops, sorry.

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:31.740
Chris, if you were looking for a red emerald late into the night, then I'm sorry.

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:33.990
It was my mistake.

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:36.910
Really?

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:38.540
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:41.040
No, it's no problem.

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:48.760
<b>Tabidatsu junbi wa dekita kai?</b>

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:48.760
<i>Are you ready to go on a journey?</i>

00:22:48.760 --> 00:22:52.010
<b>mata hitotsu asa ga kuru</b>

00:22:48.760 --> 00:22:52.010
<i>Another morning has arrived</i>

00:22:52.010 --> 00:22:55.580
<b>Atarashii shatsu ni kigaete</b>

00:22:52.010 --> 00:22:55.580
<i>Change into a new shirt</i>

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:59.040
<b>Kurayami wo nukedasou</b>

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:59.040
<i>And escape the darkness</i>

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:02.480
<b>Nemuranai machi wa kyou mo</b>

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:06.650
<i>The sleepless city quietly watches over you again today</i>

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:06.650
<b>Shizuka ni tada mimamotteiru</b>

00:23:09.430 --> 00:23:12.660
<b>Kimi to boku ga hajimatteyuku!</b>

00:23:09.430 --> 00:23:12.660
<i>We begin to go!</i>

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:16.270
<b>To be shine, To be free</b>

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:19.000
<b>Tomadowanai de</b>

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:19.000
<i>Don't be bewildered</i>

00:23:19.660 --> 00:23:25.920
<b>Toki no nami wa tsuyoku yasashii</b>

00:23:19.660 --> 00:23:25.920
<i>The waves of time are strong and kind</i>

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:30.970
<b>Sugu ni sugu ni kimi wo mukae ni yuku</b>

